{"content_hash": "e9e0ec6f8f3d8361", "version_id": 194, "article_id": 20, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies at 102", "title_zh": "奥斯卡影后伊娃·玛丽·森特去世，享年102岁", "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqze43ky1xgdo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/98d6/live/7a402d70-c229-11f1-babe-4199b0e7ccea.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-07", "word_count": 286, "reading_minutes": 1.4, "lead": "Eva Marie Saint, who won an Oscar for her very first film and later starred in a famous Hitchcock thriller, has died at the age of 102. She was one of the last surviving stars of Hollywood's golden age.", "lead_zh": "伊娃·玛丽·森特凭借第一部电影就拿下奥斯卡奖，后来又主演了希区柯克的经典惊悚片。她近日去世，享年102岁，是好莱坞黄金时代最后几位在世明星之一。", "preview": "Saint died on Tuesday of natural causes at her home in Los Angeles, surrounded by family and loved ones. A family representative, Jeff Sande", "preview_zh": "森特于周二在洛杉矶家中因自然原因去世，家人和亲友陪伴在侧。她的家庭代表杰夫·桑德森证实了这一消息。直到去世前，她都是全球最年长的在世奥斯卡奖得主。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 184, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/audio/20/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 109.7, "size_bytes": 661968, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 330, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/data/versions/194.json", "paragraphs": ["Saint died on Tuesday of natural causes at her home in Los Angeles, surrounded by family and loved ones. A family representative, Jeff Sanderson, confirmed the news. Until her death, she was the oldest surviving Oscar winner in the world.", "She won the Academy Award for best supporting actress for her movie debut in Elia Kazan's 1954 crime drama On the Waterfront. In that film she played Edie Doyle, the moral centre of the story and the love interest of Marlon Brando's troubled boxer-turned-docker.", "Five years later, she took the role of the dangerous Eve Kendall in Alfred Hitchcock's spy thriller North by Northwest, seducing Cary Grant's confused advertising executive. Saint said Hitchcock worked with her \"from the outside in\", controlling her hair, makeup, clothes and even her purse, which gave her the feeling of being a spy lady.", "Born in Newark, New Jersey in 1924, Saint had planned to become a teacher before falling in love with theatre. She trained in New York at the Actors Studio, which was co-founded by Kazan, and began her career in live television in the late 1940s. She also won an Emmy in 1990 for the TV series People Like Us.", "Saint later reduced her work while raising a family with her husband, director Jeffrey Hayden. Their marriage lasted 65 years, until his death in 2016. In her 80s she returned to the big screen as Clark Kent's adoptive mother in Superman Returns, and she continued acting into her nineties.", "She once said that growing older had made her a better actress. \"The longer you live, the smarter you get, because you've been around, you've seen things,\" she told Turner Classic Movies. Saint is survived by her two children."], "paragraphs_zh": ["森特于周二在洛杉矶家中因自然原因去世，家人和亲友陪伴在侧。她的家庭代表杰夫·桑德森证实了这一消息。直到去世前，她都是全球最年长的在世奥斯卡奖得主。", "她凭借在伊利亚·卡赞1954年犯罪剧情片《码头风云》中的电影处女作，获得奥斯卡最佳女配角奖。片中她饰演伊迪·多伊尔，是整部影片的道德核心，也是马龙·白兰度饰演的内心挣扎的拳击手转码头工人的恋人。", "五年后，她在阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克的间谍惊悚片《西北偏北》中出演危险的伊芙·肯德尔，诱惑加里·格兰特饰演的那位一头雾水的广告主管。森特说，希区柯克对她采取“由外而内”的打造方式，从发型、妆容、服装甚至手提包都亲自把控，这让她有了当间谍女人的感觉。", "森特1924年出生于新泽西州纽瓦克，原本打算当老师，后来爱上了戏剧。她在纽约的演员工作室接受训练，该工作室由卡赞联合创办，她于20世纪40年代末在电视直播节目中开始职业生涯。1990年，她还凭电视剧《我们这样的人》获得艾美奖。", "后来，森特与丈夫、导演杰弗里·海登组建家庭，逐渐减少了工作。两人的婚姻持续了65年，直到海登2016年去世。80多岁时，她重返大银幕，在2006年大片《超人归来》中饰演克拉克·肯特的养母，并一直演到90多岁。", "她曾说，年纪越大，自己越是一名好演员。她告诉特纳经典电影频道：“你活得越久，就越聪明，因为你见识多了，经历过各种事情。”森特身后留下两个孩子。"], "body": "Saint died on Tuesday of natural causes at her home in Los Angeles, surrounded by family and loved ones. A family representative, Jeff Sanderson, confirmed the news. Until her death, she was the oldest surviving Oscar winner in the world.\n\nShe won the Academy Award for best supporting actress for her movie debut in Elia Kazan's 1954 crime drama On the Waterfront. In that film she played Edie Doyle, the moral centre of the story and the love interest of Marlon Brando's troubled boxer-turned-docker.\n\nFive years later, she took the role of the dangerous Eve Kendall in Alfred Hitchcock's spy thriller North by Northwest, seducing Cary Grant's confused advertising executive. Saint said Hitchcock worked with her \"from the outside in\", controlling her hair, makeup, clothes and even her purse, which gave her the feeling of being a spy lady.\n\nBorn in Newark, New Jersey in 1924, Saint had planned to become a teacher before falling in love with theatre. She trained in New York at the Actors Studio, which was co-founded by Kazan, and began her career in live television in the late 1940s. She also won an Emmy in 1990 for the TV series People Like Us.\n\nSaint later reduced her work while raising a family with her husband, director Jeffrey Hayden. Their marriage lasted 65 years, until his death in 2016. In her 80s she returned to the big screen as Clark Kent's adoptive mother in Superman Returns, and she continued acting into her nineties.\n\nShe once said that growing older had made her a better actress. \"The longer you live, the smarter you get, because you've been around, you've seen things,\" she told Turner Classic Movies. Saint is survived by her two children.", "body_zh": "森特于周二在洛杉矶家中因自然原因去世，家人和亲友陪伴在侧。她的家庭代表杰夫·桑德森证实了这一消息。直到去世前，她都是全球最年长的在世奥斯卡奖得主。\n\n她凭借在伊利亚·卡赞1954年犯罪剧情片《码头风云》中的电影处女作，获得奥斯卡最佳女配角奖。片中她饰演伊迪·多伊尔，是整部影片的道德核心，也是马龙·白兰度饰演的内心挣扎的拳击手转码头工人的恋人。\n\n五年后，她在阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克的间谍惊悚片《西北偏北》中出演危险的伊芙·肯德尔，诱惑加里·格兰特饰演的那位一头雾水的广告主管。森特说，希区柯克对她采取“由外而内”的打造方式，从发型、妆容、服装甚至手提包都亲自把控，这让她有了当间谍女人的感觉。\n\n森特1924年出生于新泽西州纽瓦克，原本打算当老师，后来爱上了戏剧。她在纽约的演员工作室接受训练，该工作室由卡赞联合创办，她于20世纪40年代末在电视直播节目中开始职业生涯。1990年，她还凭电视剧《我们这样的人》获得艾美奖。\n\n后来，森特与丈夫、导演杰弗里·海登组建家庭，逐渐减少了工作。两人的婚姻持续了65年，直到海登2016年去世。80多岁时，她重返大银幕，在2006年大片《超人归来》中饰演克拉克·肯特的养母，并一直演到90多岁。\n\n她曾说，年纪越大，自己越是一名好演员。她告诉特纳经典电影频道：“你活得越久，就越聪明，因为你见识多了，经历过各种事情。”森特身后留下两个孩子。", "text": "Saint died on Tuesday of natural causes at her home in Los Angeles, surrounded by family and loved ones. A family representative, Jeff Sanderson, confirmed the news. Until her death, she was the oldest surviving Oscar winner in the world. She won the Academy Award for best supporting actress for her movie debut in Elia Kazan's 1954 crime drama On the Waterfront. In that film she played Edie Doyle, the moral centre of the story and the love interest of Marlon Brando's troubled boxer-turned-docker. Five years later, she took the role of the dangerous Eve Kendall in Alfred Hitchcock's spy thriller North by Northwest, seducing Cary Grant's confused advertising executive. Saint said Hitchcock worked with her \"from the outside in\", controlling her hair, makeup, clothes and even her purse, which gave her the feeling of being a spy lady. Born in Newark, New Jersey in 1924, Saint had planned to become a teacher before falling in love with theatre. She trained in New York at the Actors Studio, which was co-founded by Kazan, and began her career in live television in the late 1940s. She also won an Emmy in 1990 for the TV series People Like Us. Saint later reduced her work while raising a family with her husband, director Jeffrey Hayden. Their marriage lasted 65 years, until his death in 2016. In her 80s she returned to the big screen as Clark Kent's adoptive mother in Superman Returns, and she continued acting into her nineties. She once said that growing older had made her a better actress. \"The longer you live, the smarter you get, because you've been around, you've seen things,\" she told Turner Classic Movies. Saint is survived by her two children.", "vocab": [{"word": "surviving", "pos": "adj", "zh": "在世的；幸存的", "note": "常与 the oldest/last 连用，指某群体中仍在世的人。"}, {"word": "natural causes", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "自然原因（非外力致死）", "note": "讣闻常用语，die of natural causes。"}, {"word": "debut", "pos": "noun", "zh": "处女作；首次亮相", "note": "movie debut 指第一部电影作品。"}, {"word": "supporting actress", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "女配角", "note": "对应 best supporting actress 最佳女配角。"}, {"word": "love interest", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "恋爱对象；片中恋人", "note": "影评常用词，指剧情中的感情线角色。"}, {"word": "thriller", "pos": "noun", "zh": "惊悚片；惊险小说", "note": "spy thriller 间谍惊悚片。"}, {"word": "seduce", "pos": "verb", "zh": "诱惑；勾引", "note": "可指情感上的吸引，也可引申为引诱某人做某事。"}, {"word": "reduced her work", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "减少了工作", "note": "scale back 也有同样意思，更口语化。"}, {"word": "raise a family", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "养家；抚养孩子", "note": "常与 while 连用，表示一边做某事一边养育家庭。"}, {"word": "comeback", "pos": "noun", "zh": "复出；回归", "note": "make a comeback 重新回到公众视野。"}, {"word": "longevity", "pos": "noun", "zh": "长寿；持久", "note": "可指人的寿命，也可指事业持续时间长。"}, {"word": "is survived by", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "身后留下（亲人）", "note": "讣告固定表达，后接仍在世的家属。"}], "title_original": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies aged 102", "summary_original": "She starred opposite Marlon Brando in On the Waterfront, then alongside Cary Grant in Hitchcock's North by Northwest.", "body_original": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies aged 102\nBy\nPaul Glynn\nCulture reporter\nPublished\n7 October 2026\nEva Marie Saint, the Oscar-winning actress who starred in Hollywood classics such as On the Waterfront and North by Northwest, has died aged 102.\nSaint won the Academy Award for best supporting actress for her movie debut in director Elia Kazan's 1954 crime drama, On the Waterfront; playing Edie Doyle, the moral compass of the film and love interest of Marlon Brando's conflicted boxer-turned-docker.\nFive years later, she portrayed femme fatale Eve Kendall, dangerously seducing Cary Grant's entangled advertising executive in Alfred Hitchcock's spy thriller, North by Northwest.\nShe died on Tuesday of natural causes, surrounded by family and loved ones at her home in Los Angeles, family representative Jeff Sanderson confirmed.\nUntil her death, Saint was the oldest surviving Oscar winner and one of the last remaining stars of Hollywood's golden age.\nStarting her career in live television in the late 1940s, she also won an Emmy Award in 1990 for her career-capping role as the rich widow Lil Van Degan Altemus in People Like Us.\nBorn in Newark, New Jersey in 1924, Saint had originally intended to become a teacher before developing a passion for theatre.\nShe trained in New York at the Herbert Berghof Studio and then the Actors Studio - the home of method acting - co-founded by Kazan.\nSaint burst on to the Hollywood scene with her performance as the gentle but resolute Edie in Kazan's classic, On the Waterfront.\nHer co-star Brando was an intense method actor and Saint admitted to having found him \"adorable\" but \"a little frightening\".\n\"I felt that he could see right through me,\" she told Turner Classic Movies (TCM) in a 2013 interview.\nAccepting her Oscar trophy while nine-months pregnant, Saint quipped: \"I may have the baby right here!\".\nShe wasn't far off, having her son just two days afterwards.\nShe was considered a surprise choice, though, to play one of Hitchcock's cool and calculating heroines in his masterpiece, North by Northwest.\nThe English filmmaker was known for being very demanding of his leading ladies.\n\"He worked with me from the outside in,\" said Saint.\n\"My hair, my makeup, my shoes, my jewellery, my purse, my gloves, everything. And just from creating that exterior for me, he gave me the sense of a spy lady.\"\nCritics have argued that her character helped to create the sophisticated, sexually confident and intelligent blonde-haired archetype that many \"Bond women\", as they have been known, later followed in the 007 films.\nSaint also starred opposite Paul Newman in Otto Preminger's Exodus in 1960, and alongside Warren Beatty in John Frankenheimer's All Fall Down.\nBut she then scaled back her career while raising a family with her husband, director Jeffrey Hayden.\nHalf a century later, Saint made a big screen comeback as Clark Kent's adoptive mother in the 2006 blockbuster Superman Returns, while in her 80s.\nAnd she later had parts in the supernatural fantasy Winter's Tale, alongside Colin Farrell and Russell Crowe, and the 2019 nun drama Mariette in Ecstasy.\nThis all followed her Emmy win in 1990 for her role in the TV miniseries People Like Us, which was set among New York's high society.\nSaint, who has two stars on the Hollywood Walk of Fame for her movie and TV work, said her longevity in acting had given her work extra depth.\n\"The longer you live, the smarter you get, because you've been around, you've seen things,\" she told TCM.\n\"You've gone through different emotional experiences in your own life, and hopefully, you understand things better.\n\"And that makes you a better actress.\"\nSaint's marriage to Hayden lasted for 65 years, until his death in 2016, and she is survived by their two children.\nRelated topics\nActing\nFilm\nTelevision\nMore on this story\nParamount takes over Warner Bros in $110bn Hollywood merger\nPublished\n1 day ago\nAmazon wins global rights to stream Emmys in six-year deal\nPublished\n1 day ago\nOscars ceremony moving to new home outside Hollywood\nPublished\n26 March", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T01:14:34.129895", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Saint", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.5, "sm": 100, "em": 500, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "died", "s": 0.512, "e": 0.8, "sm": 512, "em": 799, "cs": 6, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "on", "s": 0.812, "e": 0.963, "sm": 812, "em": 962, "cs": 11, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "Tuesday", "s": 0.975, "e": 1.438, "sm": 975, "em": 1437, "cs": 14, "ce": 21, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "of", "s": 1.45, "e": 1.55, "sm": 1450, "em": 1550, "cs": 22, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "natural", "s": 1.562, "e": 2.0, "sm": 1562, "em": 2000, "cs": 25, "ce"